2026-09-23: redundant negated-truth lowering, reduced from KVM null guards.

RED: the new CLI regression compiles with zero Rust errors; its shape check
fails because null_case contains two ICmp instructions, expected one. The
original value/effect control passes. This is missed code-generation quality,
not evidence that those returned values were previously wrong.

GREEN: !integer and !pointer compare the already-evaluated full-width value
directly with zero/null. No intermediate (x != 0) boolean is needed. The
existing compare/branch fusion then applies without any MIR/SSA/validator
relaxation. Floating negation retains its unordered-truth path. Pointer null
values retain their pointer type rather than converting to integers.

Three Rust regressions PASS, including O0/O2 C-HIR/EvoIR execution, validated
IR/MIR, assembly generation, narrow/128-bit values, function pointers, numeric
boolean results, +/-zero, NaN, volatile evaluation once and short-circuiting.
Negative interpreter controls retain E3001/E3002/E3005 (uninitialized read,
division by zero, illegal shift count). They are not run as native C oracles.
Fixed sealed arm64 GCC 14.2.0-19 and Clang 19.1.7 at O0/O2 return 0; EvoCC's
O0/O2 assemblies, linked with GCC and run in the same image, also return 0.
The null_case native body shrinks from 19 to 14 instructions: the eliminated
instructions are cset, a zero materialization, two bit masks and a comparison.

Original-unit replay: virt/kvm/kvm_main.c, unchanged .o.cmd projection via
tools/k1/cmdrecord.py, including PAC, SSP sysreg/offset, auto-init, patchable
entries, debug types and -fno-strict-overflow. Sealed assembler uses the
recorded -Wa,-march=armv8.5-a. No object is installed and no Image is relinked.
Controlled prior/current compiler comparison on those identical inputs:
                       text       data     bss
before                243232     14005     168
after                 237968     14005     168
Global symbol names/types are identical. Both assemblers emit the same five
existing zero-length .space warnings. The older installed Image object has
text=291804 but includes other compiler differences; do not attribute that
larger reduction to this patch. Full K02 runtime remains OPEN.

Changed gate against 6eeee66: 1094 PASS, 0 FAIL, 3 existing ignored tests,
123 groups across evocc/evocc-eqopt/evocc-lower/evocc-policy/evocc-proofcheck/
evocc-randgate. Clippy -D warnings and workspace fmt check PASS. This is the
affected-crate gate, not a new complete kernel/application campaign.

